e they iterate in lockstep due to barriers? Actually there is a barrier at end of each iteration, so after the barrier, all threads proceed to next iter with same value (since they all increment). So it's fine.\n\nNow produce JSON response with file content and transformations list.\n\nWe'll set sources_kept to [] since integration_source_ids empty.\n\nTransformations: [\"Double buffering using alternating arrays\", \"Manual OpenMP thread partitioning instead of worksharing loop\", \"Explicit barrier for synchronization\"].\n\nHypothesis: Using double-buffered body arrays and manual per-thread index partitioning (stride by number of threads) eliminates data races, reduces worksharing scheduling overhead, and preserves deterministic per-body accumulation order, improving performance on 4 cores.\n\nNotes: Mention that we avoid SIMD to preserve exact floating-point order.\n\nLet's output."
